(footprint "RotaryEncoder_Alps_EC05E1220401_SMD"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Alps Alpine EC05E1220401 5 mm hollow-shaft encoder, vertical SMD, 12 pulse / 12 detent, hex hole 1.72 mm (1.73 mm lead-in at the top). Origin = bore centre. Pads, peg holes and the shaft cutout follow Alps EC catalog drawing No.3 (checked against LCSC C116648's EasyEDA land). The Edge.Cuts cutout covers Alps' 3.0 mm R0.3 hole, sized for a 1 mm router (R0.5 corners) and stretched to 2.35 mm on the far side to clear the part's second pair of pegs and the drum, which sits below the base. It also lets the maclock dial's tapered shaft go about 1 mm into the board, where the bore grips it.")
	(tags "encoder rotary Alps EC05E hollow shaft hex vertical mouse wheel")
